{"id":2894,"date":"2021-05-26T14:40:35","date_gmt":"2021-05-26T21:40:35","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=2894"},"modified":"2024-09-01T13:37:25","modified_gmt":"2024-09-01T20:37:25","slug":"how-to-use-blockly","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/how-to-use-blockly\/","title":{"rendered":"1.1: How to Use Blockly"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2214cf5d25c\" name=\"6a2214cf5d25c\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>What is Blockly?<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Blockly is an online application that you can access right from your web\u00a0 browser. However, with Zumi, we will be accessing Blockly from her computer. With Blockly, you can pair to your Zumi as well as program it in three modes:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Junior: Simplified block-based coding for beginners.<\/li>\n<li>Senior: For intermediate coders who have some familiarity with block coding.<\/li>\n<li>Master: Text-based coding in Python for advanced students. This is currently not available. Check back for updates!<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;3534&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2214cf5d38c\" name=\"6a2214cf5d38c\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Write your code<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]To write your code, drag blocks from the menus on the left to the workspace in the middle of the page. Connect blocks like puzzle pieces to create a list of commands in a specific order. Remember, <strong>code runs from top to bottom<\/strong>; therefore, Zumi will first attempt to do the command at the top and then she will move on to the next one. She will repeat this process until she reaches the last line of your code, which is when she will stop.<\/p>\n<p>As an example, Zumi will first move forward for 1 second at a speed of 40. After she completes that, then she will turn right 90 degrees. Since there are no commands after that, she &#8211; and the code (!) &#8211; will stop.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;3529&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]To delete blocks, separate what you want to get rid of from your code and drag them to the trashcan in the lower righthand corner. If you want to delete your entire program, you can drag the whole thing to the trashcan.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;3530&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]To see what your program looks like in Python, click on one of the Python language icon on the right side of the workspace.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;3531&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]Make sure you save! You can do this by going to the menu in the upper lefthand corner of the workspace and clicking on &#8220;Save&#8221;. To open a saved program, go to the same menu and click on &#8220;Open&#8230;&#8221;.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;462&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2214cf5d3e9\" name=\"6a2214cf5d3e9\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Run your code<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Click on &#8220;Run code&#8221; in the upper left hand side of your workspace to get your Zumi driving with your code! If you need to stop your Zumi for any reason during its drive, click on &#8220;Stop&#8221;, which is right next to the &#8220;Run code&#8221; button.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;464&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 4 What is Blockly? [vc_column_text]Blockly is an online application that you can access right from your web\u00a0 browser. However, with Zumi, we will be accessing Blockly from her&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/how-to-use-blockly\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":2899,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":2878,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[],"lesson-tag":[],"class_list":["post-2894","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","module-getting-started","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/2894","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":10,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/2894\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":11747,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/2894\/revisions\/11747"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/2899"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=2894"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=2894"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/w